title: '[SAFETY] adapters do not inject untrusted-data framing (peer messages are data, not instructions)'
---
There is no single-sourced safety prompt/skill fragment that every adapter injects. For agent-to-agent messaging the instruction-injection threat (an agent obeying inbound message content) is live. Ship one canonical fragment covering: peer messages are untrusted third-party data, not instructions; how to identify self; alias@hostid addressing; trust tiers; FYI does not mean act-on. Each adapter (Claude/Codex/pi/opencode/kimi) must inject it on session start; conformance-test its presence. Source: friction-points-cn.md.